    "https://cugcareers.coventry.ac.uk/job/Coventry-Lecturer-%28Teaching%29-in-Physiotherapy-Cove-cv1/1372686057/": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Teaching) in Physiotherapy Job Details",
      "description": "Lecturer (Teaching) in Physiotherapy Job Details | coventryun We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Locations Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Category All Faculty/Business Area All Location All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Job Title Lecturer (Teaching) in Physiotherapy Job Reference 3789 Application Closing Date 19/10/2026 Division, Department CUHC CU Health and Care Limited (CUHC) ,AHP Physiotherapy Salary Competitive starting salary range from £39,324 up to £44,710 (dependent on experience) with the potential to progress. A discretionary range for candidates with exceptional experience can be discussed/considered. Mode Permanent , Full Time Our Mission Coventry University Group is a global education provider dedicated to Creating Better Futures. We are driven by the belief that through education, equity, and innovation, we empower our students, people, and communities to transform their lives. Central to our 2030 Strategy is the ambitious growth of our School of Health and Care to meet the evolving health needs of the future locally, nationally, and globally. To enable this, our School has evolved into Coventry University Health and Care Limited. This agile, autonomous structure allows us to push boundaries and foster closer partnerships, enabling us to scale our provision and widen access to rewarding careers across the health and social care sector. The Role An exciting opportunity has arisen to join our thoughtful and dedicated physiotherapy team as a Lecturer (Teaching). Our well-established pre-registration courses, delivered across different campus sites, offer a range of routes into the profession including direct entry and apprenticeships; undergraduate and postgraduate. Our focus is on developing reflective, compassionate, and highly skilled physiotherapists, whilst fostering excellence, innovation, and leadership in physiotherapy education and training. As Lecturer (Teaching) in Physiotherapy you will undertake teaching and course co-ordination with a focus on further developing new and innovative academic practice and learning opportunities working in collaboration with our partners. You will work as part of the course team supporting the development and delivery of undergraduate, postgraduate, and professional programs including apprenticeship routes ensuring learners have an effective learning experience. Based within the AHP Physiotherapy you will work with academic colleagues across CUHC to enrich learning and teaching experience to ensure relevant aspects of research, enterprise and professional context are embedded in modules and courses. Duties include: Lead the curation, adaptation, design and development of module(s) and course teaching materials and contributing to ongoing curriculum development including practice-based learning. Leading moderation and quality assurance of appropriate module assessment. Teaching on modules and courses at HE levels 4-7 and our Level 6 physiotherapist apprenticeship, and leading teams of teaching staff. Contributing to the effective delivery and quality assurance of BSc and MSc provision. Liaison with external stakeholders as required, including employers and practice partners Qualifications Required Essential Master’s degree in appropriate subject or Honours Degree with appropriate professional qualification and/or membership Current registration with the HCPC as Physiotherapist A teaching qualification or acceptance of the requirement to acquire one Experience of delivering physiotherapy education (professional/university/apprenticeship) Desirable PhD Active membership of appropriate professional body (The Chartered Society of Physiotherapy) Our Successful Candidate You will bring substantial clinical experience and specialist expertise in neuro physiotherapy and neurological rehabilitation or cardiorespiratory physiotherapy, enabling you to deliver high‑quality teaching and mentorship. You will have demonstrable experience of successful teaching and learning at higher education levels 4-7 in Physiotherapy either in higher education or within a clinical environment. You can demonstrate high standards of teaching, learning and student engagement consistent with our reputation and track record as a high-quality provider of teaching and learning. You will have experience of supporting learning within your role and of providing high quality academic and pastoral support to students and/or professionals. You will be enthusiastic and self-motivated, experienced in supporting, enhancing and engaging in an ‘active learning’ pedagogy with evidence in proactively supporting student success. As a global education provider, you will hold experience and awareness of learner’s cultural differences and expectations with the ability to effectively communicate with a wide range of people from diverse backgrounds. Innovation and collaboration are key to our success, therefore the ability to generate and follow through innovative ideas, work both independently and part of a wider team with the willingness to engage in flexible ways of working are key skills required for this role. The Benefits Along with a competitive salary we offer an industry leading Rewards and Benefits package which includes: Excellent Employers Pension Contribution 30 days Annual leave plus Bank Holidays New Holiday Purchase Scheme up to 5 additional days Life Assurance 4x Salary BUPA Cash Plan 50% off Tuition Fees for staff dependants CU Reward Scheme – Discounts across a range of High Street/ Online Retailers Cycle To Work scheme Our Culture As a global Education Group, equality, diversity, and inclusion are embedded within the fabric of our organisation and are a key focus of our core values. We harness the power and potential of the diverse cultures, backgrounds, abilities, and experiences of our students, colleagues, and partners to create opportunities for all. Full Job Description & Person Specification Click here to view the full job description and person specification We look forward to hearing from you! Please enable JavaScript Screen readers cannot read the following searchable map. Follow this link to reach our Job Search page to search for available jobs in a more accessible format. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Coventry Home View All Jobs Website Privacy Notice Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are